OpenJazz for AmigaOS 3.x (AmiCradle)
====================================

OpenJazz is AJ Thomson's and Carsten Teibes's open-source engine for Jazz
Jackrabbit (Epic MegaGames, 1994). This drawer holds the engine built for a
68040 or 68060 with an FPU. Status: TESTING, not a release.

Requirements
------------

- AmigaOS 3.2, a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU, an RTG board.
- GFOpenGPU's SDL2.module in LIBS:GFOpenGPU/, and AHI for sound.
- Jazz Jackrabbit's data: the shareware episode or your own full game.
  It is not part of this archive.

Installing
----------

Unpack the archive anywhere and double-click Install-OpenJazz: it checks
the CPU, the FPU and SDL2.module, asks where the game goes (Work:Games by
default) and copies the OpenJazz drawer there. Then copy the Jazz
Jackrabbit data files into the OpenJazz drawer, beside the program. The
settings (openjazz.cfg) are written there too; installing again over it
keeps them and your data files.

Playing
-------

Double-click OpenJazz. The arrow keys move, Space jumps, Left Alt fires, Enter
chooses in the menus and Escape goes back.

Licence
-------

OpenJazz is GPL-2.0-or-later (COPYING); the source is at
https://github.com/AlisterT/openjazz and the port at
https://github.com/DalsinAI/amigaopenjazz. Jazz Jackrabbit and its data
belong to Epic Games. The icons are drawn for this build from the engine's
own icon.
